<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Info.plist for Roost-Iced.app — M6 6a evaluation bundle.

  `mac/scripts/bundle-iced.sh` copies this file into the .app bundle
  and substitutes @VERSION@ with the workspace version (see
  `roost_workspace_version` in bundle-lib.sh). This bundle exists so
  the iced UI (`crates/roost-iced`) can be evaluated against the
  Swift app side by side: Sparkle (6c), UNUserNotificationCenter
  (6e), and TCC testing all require a bundled, signed .app — see
  `docs/development/iced-migration-roadmap.md` § M6.

  Distinct identity from Roost.app (Info.plist.template) so the two
  can be installed and run in parallel: CFBundleIdentifier carries a
  `.iced` suffix, and CFBundleName/CFBundleDisplayName/
  CFBundleExecutable are "Roost-Iced" so Dock/Cmd-Tab/Finder show
  them as separate apps and `pgrep/pkill -x Roost` can never hit this
  process. `app_label` on the wire stays `Roost-iced` (roost-ipc's
  BundleProfile, untouched by this plist).

  Sparkle (M6 6c, plan 028): the update MECHANICS ship — bundle-iced.sh
  embeds + strictly signs Sparkle.framework — but NO SUFeedURL and NO
  SUPublicEDKey, by design. A build with no feed never checks, so a
  public key in today's builds buys nothing, and the two apps must
  never be able to offer each other's updates — an iced bundle
  carrying the Swift app's feed URL/key could install a
  Swift-app-shaped update over an iced binary (or vice versa). At
  enablement time the design mandates a SEPARATE feed URL and a
  SEPARATE EdDSA keypair from the Swift app's
  (charliek.github.io/roost/appcast.xml + its SUPublicEDKey stay
  Swift-only). SUEnableAutomaticChecks is present and false: with the
  updater instantiated, an ABSENT key would trigger Sparkle's
  first-run "check automatically?" permission prompt — the explicit
  false suppresses scheduled checks and that prompt; checks stay
  strictly user-invoked. Enablement recipe: set both
  ROOST_ICED_SPARKLE_FEED_URL and ROOST_ICED_SPARKLE_ED_PUBLIC_KEY at
  bundle time and bundle-iced.sh PlistBuddy-inserts the two keys into
  the stamped plist (exactly one set is a hard error; see
  roost_insert_sparkle_feed in bundle-lib.sh).

  Device-permission purpose strings (NSMicrophone/Camera/AppleEvents
  UsageDescription): paired with the capture entitlements in
  Roost-Iced.entitlements. macOS shows these when a program hosted in
  a Roost-Iced tab requests the microphone/camera (the request is
  attributed to Roost-Iced, the TCC responsible app). Both must be
  present — the entitlement to permit the request under the hardened
  runtime, the string for the prompt — matching Roost.app, ghostty,
  and cmux.

  Icon: reuses the same AppIcon art as Roost.app (shared art is a
  recorded decision, plan 027 § W2) — the display name is what
  disambiguates the Dock tile until a distinct Roost-Iced icon exists
  (future work).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>CFBundleDevelopmentRegion</key>
  <string>en</string>
  <key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
  <string>ai.stridelabs.Roost.iced</string>
  <key>CFBundleName</key>
  <string>Roost-Iced</string>
  <key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
  <string>Roost-Iced</string>
  <key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
  <string>Roost-Iced</string>
  <key>CFBundleIconFile</key>
  <string>AppIcon</string>
  <key>CFBundleIconName</key>
  <string>AppIcon</string>
  <key>CFBundleVersion</key>
  <string>@VERSION@</string>
  <key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
  <string>@VERSION@</string>
  <key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
  <string>APPL</string>
  <key>CFBundleSignature</key>
  <string>????</string>
  <key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key>
  <string>15.0</string>
  <key>NSHighResolutionCapable</key>
  <true/>
  <key>NSPrincipalClass</key>
  <string>NSApplication</string>
  <key>NSSupportsAutomaticGraphicsSwitching</key>
  <true/>
  <key>LSUIElement</key>
  <false/>
  <key>SUEnableAutomaticChecks</key>
  <false/>
  <key>NSHumanReadableCopyright</key>
  <string>Copyright © 2026 Charlie Knudsen. MIT-licensed.</string>
  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>A program running in Roost-Iced would like to use the microphone.</string>
  <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
  <string>A program running in Roost-Iced would like to use the camera.</string>
  <key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
  <string>A program running in Roost-Iced would like to use AppleScript.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
